docker build -t fairy-bake:v1 .

### Understand the command:

docker build: builds an image.
-t fairy-bake:v1: assigns the image name and tag.
.: uses the current directory as the build context.

## Check the image:
docker images

At this stage, the image exists in Docker on your EC2 host.

However, KIND runs Kubernetes nodes inside separate Docker containers. Those nodes do not automatically have access to every image in the host's local image store.

We need to make the image available to the KIND cluster.

